  "costUsd": null,
  "content": "Owen has finished strong, but his strokes gained is still well behind the Tour baseline, and approach play is the main reason.\n\n- **Scoring:** He averaged 76.0 over his last ten rounds, 9 June to 26 September. His last two rounds were qualifiers at the home course, a 74 and a 71. His 82 at Poplar Grove on 8 July is the high point of the window. Over his 14 rounds in the stats cache he averages 4.43 over par.\n- **Strokes gained:** He is at -6.74 per round over 8 rounds, against -5.82 for the team. That ranks him 5th of 7. Level: no college figure. Tour: the baseline is 0.\n- **Approach:** At -4.16 per round he ranks 6th of 7, and the team figure is -3.09. This is his biggest loss. GIR is 61.11% over 144 holes, which is 5th of 7 on the team. The Division I average is 60% and the Tour figure is 66%.\n- **Putting:** At -2.06 per round he ranks 2nd of 7, and the team figure is -3.03. Putting is a relative strength for him.\n- **Off the tee and around the green:** Off the tee he is at -0.32, 6th of 7. Around the green he is at -0.2, 4th of 7.\n\nHis last recorded round was 26 September, so there is a six-week gap with no data. The strokes gained figures rest on 8 rounds, because the two newest qualifier rounds were posted as totals only. The 71 and 74 are real scores, but I can't say how they were produced.",
